{
  "source": "Mechel (2008) Table 3, PDF pages 544-545 (printed pp. 529-530)",
  "about": "Thirty-eight rows in the three groups the page prints as italic headings: construction materials, plastics and metals. Columns: density, the modulus in MN/m2, f_cr.d in Hz m, Z_m and the loss factor. There is no Poisson ratio and no wave speed, so a row gives the bar speed through its modulus and its density and stops there: the plate and bulk speeds need a Poisson ratio this page does not print, and assuming one would attribute a number to Mechel that he did not give. What does cross to the other books is f_cr.d, the same material constant Hopkins prints as h.f_c, which printed page 531 calls out in so many words. Z_m is not held here: it is the wall impedance ratio of Eq. (11), a derived quantity rather than a property of the material, and the one row whose printed Z_m does not follow from that equation carries the discrepancy in its note and an entry in the errata registry.",
